{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 1: a snowman",
 "summary": "Geometry nodes on an object (a Geometry Nodes modifier): Mesh Primitives (UV Sphere) replacing the cube, Transform Geometry to move and scale, Join Geometry to combine three spheres into a snowman and a Grid as the ground, Set Shade Smooth and Set Material after the join, all to the Group Output; a snow material (two noise textures mixed, a light blue-to-white ramp, a bump). Beyond the tutorial, in the same node tree: a cone carrot nose, coal eyes and buttons instanced on a Mesh Line's points, twig arms and a felt hat, each with its own Set Material, under a sky.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "Snowman",
   "description": "the geometry-nodes snowman"
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "A three-ball snowman with a carrot nose, coal eyes and buttons, twig arms and a black hat, standing on a snowy square under a winter sky.",
